# FDF Portal E2E Testing Standards (Playwright)

## Core Rule

> A feature is **not complete** when its user-visible behavior has changed but its Playwright E2E coverage has not been updated.

Any implementation that creates or modifies a user-visible action or workflow **must** create or update the corresponding Playwright E2E tests.

## Playwright Skills

For browser interaction, test debugging, and advanced Playwright capabilities, use:
- `.agents/skills/playwright-dev/SKILL.md` — development and test writing
- `.agents/skills/playwright-test-results/SKILL.md` — analyzing test results
- `.agents/skills/playwright-triage/SKILL.md` — debugging failures
- `.agents/skills/playwright-devops/SKILL.md` — CI/CD integration

## Scope: When to Write or Update Tests

Tests are required for changes to:

### Authentication & Authorization
- Director Google Sign-In flow
- Director email/password login
- Signup and consent flows
- Session expiry behaviour
- IDOR and ownership enforcement

### CRUD Operations
- Group management (create, view, update)
- Roster management (add/edit/remove members)
- Chaperone management

### Forms
- Required field validation
- Format validation (email, date of birth, etc.)
- Server-side error surfacing
- Submission success/failure

### Navigation
- Route transitions
- Director-specific navigation
- Role-based navigation visibility

### Data Interactions
- Roster filtering and search
- Group roster table interactions
- File uploads (when applicable)

### Security
- IDOR tests — Directors must not access other Directors' groups
- Authorization boundary tests

## Test Architecture

```
e2e/
  auth/               — director login, signup, consent, session
  groups/             — my groups, group detail, roster management
  security/           — IDOR tests, authorization boundary tests
  fixtures/           — authentication state files, test data
  support/            — page objects, helpers, auth utilities
```

## Selectors

Prefer in this order:
1. `getByRole()` — semantic role + accessible name
2. `getByLabel()` — form field labels
3. `getByText()` — visible text content
4. `getByTestId()` — only where above cannot uniquely identify

Never use brittle CSS class selectors that encode implementation details.

## Authentication Strategy

- Use `storageState` fixtures to avoid re-authenticating in every test.
- Maintain auth state files per test user under `e2e/fixtures/`.
- Tests that validate auth itself must perform the full login flow.

## Test Environment Rules

- **Never run destructive tests against the production database.**
- Tests must be deterministic — no dependency on ambient database state.
- Use seeded test data and controlled fixtures.
- Document the test environment prerequisites in `e2e/README.md`.

## Running Tests

```bash
npm run e2e              # Portal tests on Chromium desktop
npm run e2e:mobile       # Portal mobile tests
npm run e2e:all          # All portal browser projects
```

## Backend Completion Gate

For backend/API/database changes:
- [ ] Authentication enforced where required
- [ ] Authorization enforced server-side (group ownership validated)
- [ ] IDOR tests pass (Directors cannot access other Directors' data)
- [ ] SQL parameterized (no concatenation)
- [ ] Input validation present
- [ ] PII minimized in API responses
- [ ] PII absent from logs
- [ ] Relevant Playwright E2E tests pass
- [ ] OWASP security review performed (see `fdf-security.mdc`)
